Today I solved leetcode question 896:Monotonic Array.

Description: It states that we are given an array.
              If that array is monotonic increasing (i.e for indexes i and j array[i]<=array[j]) or monotonic decreasing (i.e for indexes i and j array[i]>=array[j])
              then we must return true and if not then we must return false.
              eg- array=[1,2,2,3] true
                  array=[1,3,2] false

Solution: First we create a boolean variable increasing. And we will assign it false value.
          Then we will start our for loop.
          And if current number is smaller than previous number then we will make increasing as true.
          Else we will keep it as it is.
          Now we will check if increasing is true or not.
          If it is true then we will start our for loop and if a number is smaller than its previous one then we will return false.
          Else we will start for loop and if previous number is greater than previous one then we will return false.
          Otherwise we will return true.
